WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.120
It's that time again. Welcome to Tesla Short's Time. Daily episode 482. I'm Patrick

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:13.160
in Vancouver. Today is May 24th, 2026. There's a lot to cover in Tesla Land today. Looking

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:21.540
back at six episodes from 2026, May 18th, to 2026, May 24th, the stories that mattered

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:27.000
what we learned and what to watch next. Tesla acknowledged limits in its current vehicle

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.460
hardware for certain advanced functions. The admission points to broader industry questions

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:38.260
about how quickly cars can be upgraded for full autonomy. Suppliers and regulators are now

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.900
watching how Tesla balances software ambitions with physical constraints. The move highlights

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:49.320
tension between software goals and existing vehicle hardware. Questions now turn to upgrade

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.940
timelines across the supply chain and regulatory landscape. While hardware constraints shape

00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:00.620
what is possible today, Tesla's global manufacturing plans are also hitting external roadblocks.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:07.040
Tesla has abandoned its proposed manufacturing facility in India after facing multiple regulatory

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.680
and logistical obstacles. The decision removes a key piece of the company's strategy for deeper

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:18.200
penetration into one of the world's fastest growing auto markets. Without local production,

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:23.500
Tesla will continue relying on imports that carry higher costs and potential tariff exposure.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:30.020
The move leaves the company dependent on shipments from other regions. Sales efforts in India will

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:35.840
now operate without the cost advantages of domestic assembly. With India expansion paused,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:42.080
attention turns to how Tesla is adjusting software offerings in other regions to support sales.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:47.900
New buyers in Europe can now access full self-driving only through a monthly subscription.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:53.220
Just two countries have so far approved supervised full self-driving operation.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.920
The policy shift removes the previous outright purchase path that existed in other markets.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:05.400
Tesla is aligning payment structure with regulatory approval timelines rather than hardware capability

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:11.540
alone. Subscription uptake will become the next data point once additional countries clear the

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:17.300
software. As Europe moves to subscriptions, Tesla is simultaneously rolling out the same

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:23.060
supervised software in China to lift demand. Tesla has begun rolling out its supervised

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:29.360
full self-driving software in China. The expansion aims to improve the appeal of its vehicles amid

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:35.260
slowing domestic demand. Regulators and local infrastructure will determine how quickly the

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:41.100
feature gains traction with buyers. The rollout represents a direct attempt to use autonomy features

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:46.680
as a sales lever. Successful hinge on approvals and supporting road systems in key cities.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:52.760
While software is being tested in new markets, physical Robotaxi hardware is already appearing on

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:59.120
roads in the United States. Multiple model-wide vehicles configured for Robotaxi duty were photographed

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:04.760
in Florida, carrying updated sensor and compute hardware not present on current customer cars.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:10.640
The sightings indicate Tesla is already running supervised autonomy fleets on production like

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:16.800
vehicles ahead of wider deployment. Observers noted differences in camera placement and roofline

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:23.020
hardware consistent with next-generation hardware revisions. The activity points to ongoing validation

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:29.400
work in a new geographic market. Testing indicates Tesla is validating autonomy fleets in additional

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:36.160
regions. Hardware progress for Robotaxi contrasts with a more immediate operational issue at home.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.140
The recall targets vehicles that may lack a required certification sticker on the driver's side

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:47.860
door. Tesla identified the issue through internal checks and will remedy affected units at service

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:53.780
centers. The scope remains narrow compared with earlier camera-related recalls but still requires

00:03:53.780 --> 00:04:02.080
owner notification. 14,575 model-wide SUVs are involved. Fixes will be handled through

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:07.140
standard service channels without broader production changes. While recalls are handled through

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:12.520
normal service channels, some owners are testing advertised features in less conventional ways.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:18.580
A driver took a cyber truck into grapevine lakes specifically to test the Wade mode feature

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:24.940
and ended up facing charges for violating water safety rules. The incident shows how owners are

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:30.540
pushing the truck's advertised capabilities in real conditions. It also raises questions about how

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:36.660
Tesla communicates limits for off-road and water features. The driver entered the water deliberately

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:42.760
to evaluate the capability. Charges followed after the vehicle violated established safety boundaries.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:49.140
Real-world owner behavior sits alongside more measured product updates, such as refreshed

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:55.500
model S and X variants. A follow-up post from Tesla offered additional views of the signature

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:01.420
edition vehicles and confirmed the live-stream timing for the Fremont event. The timing suggests an

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:07.140
effort to maintain visibility for the refreshed models amid broader line-up changes. Customers

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:12.620
watching the stream will see the final handovers in real time. Additional images of the signature

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:18.480
addition model S and model X were released ahead of the deliveries. The event keeps focus on the

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:24.240
refreshed flagships during a period of wider product shifts. While flagship models receive

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:30.480
attention, Tesla is also quietly exploring service presence in new cities. Tesla has expressed

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:36.140
interest in establishing a showroom and service center in Hydeabad. The interest comes despite the

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:42.620
earlier cancellation of local manufacturing plans. Focus appears to be on sales and after-sales support

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:48.600
rather than local manufacturing. The move continues the thread of adapting market strategy without

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:54.420
local production. Physical presence would support vehicle imports and owner servicing in the region.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.100
There is a challenge worth discussing around how quickly hardware upgrades can reach the installed

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:05.780
base. Tesla's admission on current vehicle limits comes at a time when autonomy ambitions

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:11.980
remain central to future plans. The company continues to refine software on existing fleets while

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:18.400
preparing next-generation hardware for robotaxi use. Regulators in multiple regions are watching the

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:24.400
balance between capability claims and physical constraints. This week showed that software expansion

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:30.520
in China and Europe is moving ahead even as hardware questions persist. Tomorrow we'll be watching

